<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick III, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1415">1415</a>–<a href="/years/1493">1493</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick III was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> duke of Inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> who became King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 1440 and the last emperor crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in 1452. In 1453 he confirmed the forged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/privilegium-maius">Privilegium Maius</a>, giving the Habsburgs the title of archduke. His long reign was beset by rebellion and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a>, but he raised loyal lords to higher rank and arranged his son Maximilian's Burgundian marriage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Frederick III, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Burgkmair the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hans_Burgkmair_d._%C3%84._005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
